ster.cljc:882:;; As the stack kernel: a positional closure lifts by the offset table row\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:918:  (lift-closure [vm closure encode]\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:919:    (let [[ident rel] (or (image-pc vm (:body-pc closure))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:923:      (cond-> {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/closure,\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:928:               :yin.k/arity (:arity closure),\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:929:               :yin.k/frames (mapv #(mapv encode %) (:frames closure))}\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:930:        (:store-of closure) (assoc :yin.k/store-of (:store-of closure)))))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:931:  (lower-closure [vm marker decode]\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:940:      ;; the arity is that of a `:closure` of the attached code whose body\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:942:      (when-not (some #(and (= :closure (nth % 0))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:947:      (values/closure\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:949:        (cond-> {:type :closure,\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:493:;; Carrier lifecycle: lift, pin, heap, closure and continuation images\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:568:(deftest closure-and-continuation-images-keep-float64-content-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:585:  (testing \\\\\\\"a closure whose environment holds every special float: the\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:587:            closure lowered into another task returns them unchanged, on\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:598:          (is (values/closure? f) (str k))\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_conv_test.cljc:3:   checks of str, repr, print and int(str), and the deferred numeric\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_conv_test.cljc:191:(deftest deferred-items-test\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:11:   (depth + position), `:load-free` (name), and `:closure` (arity + body\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:56:   closures carry an arity and body pc.\\\\\\\"\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:58:   :closure [[:yin.debruijn.code/arity :uint] [:yin.debruijn.code/body :pc]],\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:703:   operands (jump/branch-false targets, closure bodies) are rejected\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:722:   collecting the `[body-pc chain]` of every nested :closure this walk\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:723:   passes through -- a :closure instruction's own body is a different\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:725:   continues past the :closure instruction itself into the rest of this\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:730:   second :closure declaration -- stops the walk and reports that pc as\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:748:              nested' (if (= :closure op)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:760:   :closure's declared body -- the S3 scope resolver's own data, built\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:766:   Two :closure instructions -- anywhere in the image, in either order,\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:798:   Two :closure instructions declaring different arities for the same\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:1157:  \\\\\\\"Node count of a continuation payload; closures, continuations and cell\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:1218:  \\\\\\\"Node count of `x` with continuation and closure payloads followed; a\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:115:**Purpose:** The owner tag every closure and continuation this task mints carries (D7), derived once from the capability secret by `yin.vm.values/owner-tag` in `yin.vm/empty-state` and never revealing it. A task composed without a secret has owner nil. Application and invocation refuse a closure or continuation whose owner is not this task's (`:foreign-value`); the lift encoder refuses one as `:yin.k/non-portable`, and `lower