/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn`; H0's acceptance is\\\\n352: that the committed output lists exactly the 142/140/141 files above, and\\\\n353: that the two traversals (the committed tool and the r3 reviewer's method)\\\\n354: agree, recorded in the slice report. Until that lands, the totals here are\\\\n355: R.\\\\n356: \\\\n357: Classification of every file in the closure that has any host contact (the\\\\n358: remaining files have none beyond §3.3 syntax; the committed H0 output marks\\\\n359: each file with its class, which is what makes \\\\\\\"remaining\\\\\\\" checkable):\\\\n360: \\\\n361: +-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\\\\n362: | Namespaces                                          | Contact (V)                            | Class and slice                                          |\\\\n363: +=====================================================+========================================+==========================================================+\\\\n364: | `yin.vm.integer.host`, `dao.jing.cbor` (helpers,    | Big integers, floats, Decimal/Ratio,   | Internal pure: profile. H1-H2 (writer: H4).              |\\\\n365: | carriers, Decimal/Ratio, float bits, writer),       | NFC, bytes, code units, host arrays    |                                                          |\\\\n366: | `dao.jing.cbor.boring`, `dao.jing.cbor.cljd`,       |                                        |                                                          |\\\\n367: | `yin.vm.debruijn`, `yin.vm.debruijn-code`,          |                                        |                                                          |\\\\n368: | `yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.values`,                     |                                        |                                                          |\\\\n369: | `dao.stream.chunks`, `dao.stream.base64`,           |                       