sign` require  | Green; counts unchanged plus `dao.host.hash-test`; every corpus   |\\\\n736: |       | +migr. | them (`generate` stays, deferred). The string hash forms and `sign`'s `utf8`   | address identical; `sign_test` 4/4; `base64_test` 3/3 on three    |\\\\n737: |       |        | switch to `text/utf8-encode`: a **named behaviour change** for strings with an | lanes; a direct test that `digest-string` and `message` refuse an |\\\\n738: |       |        | unpaired surrogate (refusal instead of a substituted byte), recorded in the    | unpaired-surrogate string; **host-library gate (§8.2)**: within   |\\\\n739: |       |        | slice report; such strings are already refused by the canonical codec (corpus  | the adopted closure, no executable reference to `MessageDigest`,  |\\\\n740: |       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,               |\\\\n741: |       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` outside `dao/host/`, and   |\\\\n742: |       |        |                                                                                | for the Ed25519 names outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`           |\\\\n743: |       |        |                                                                                | (`generate`); scan errors reported distinctly.                    |\\\\n744: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\n745: | H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\\\\n746: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\\\\n747: |       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\\\\n748: |       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\\\\n749: |       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\\\\n750: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\n751: \\\\n752: Dependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\\\\n753: \\\\n754: ### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\\\\n755: \\\\n756: The gate never promises \\\\\\\"no arms across `src/cljc`\\\\\\\", only \\\\\\\"no non-exempt\\\\n757: arms outside list 1\\\\\\\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\\\\n758: closure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\\\\n759: the **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\\\\n760: difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\\\\n761: is today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\\\\n762: (five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\\\\n763: marked as such in the table.\\\\n764: \\\\n765: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n766: | Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\\\\n767: +============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\\\\n768: | H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\\\\n769: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (the Dart Jing writer; a lane-specific file counted here,    | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\\\\n770: |                            | not under seams), `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,           | stays for `generate` only;  |\\\\n771: |                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as  | three of these files are    |\\\\n772: |                            | exempt protocol syntax), `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`,                    | deleted (§8.1 paragraph).   |\\\\n773: |                            | `dao/jing/dht.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc` (bytes arms only).        |                             |\\\\n774: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n775: | Profile (the arms belong   | Baseline: `dao/data/arrays.cljc`. Planned additions, not in the H0 baseline:                    | Stay; the seven additions   |\\\\n776: | here by design)            | `dao/host/{integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign}.cljc` (P; five join list 1 at H1, two at  | are on list 1 from the      |\\\\n777: |                            | H3).                                                                                            | slice that creates them.    |\\\\n778: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n779: | Retained runtime           | `dao/data/btree.cljc` (atomic flag `:102-119`, weak and soft references `:212-245`: substantive | Stay, with the table C      |\\\\n780: | prerequisites (table C)    | arms, not protocol syntax, retained by design); `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc` (promise facade,  | reason recorded in the      |\\\\n781: |                            | deferred §9.1); `dao/pretty.cljc` (`StringWriter`/pprint, display only, §3.1).                  | gate's list.                |\\\\n782: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n783: | Codec-track files          | `dao/stream/ws.cljc`, `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,            | Stay; owned by that track;  |\\\\n784: | (untouched by this track)  | `remote_channel.cljc`, `ws_project.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`.                                   | `codec.cljc:45` after C4.   |\\\\n785: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n786: | Seams and driver           | `src/clj`, `src/cljs`, `src/cljd` seam and shadow files (§3.1 lane-specific list) **except**    | Stay, except the Dart Jing  |\\\\n787: |                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`, which is a Jing writer H4 deletes, not a seam; it is on the | writer, deleted in H4.      |\\\\n788: |                            | baseline under the first row's `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` twin. `yin/repl/main.cljc`,          |                             |\\\\n789: |                            | `yin/repl/host.cljc`, `yin/repl/state.cljc`.                                                    |                             |\\\\n790: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n791: | Deferred-scope files (§9)  | `dao/jing/file.cljc`, `dao/space/store/fs.cljc`, `dao/space/store.cljc`,                        | Stay until the deferred     |\\\\n792: |                            | `dao/stream/journal/file.cljc`, `dao/jing/content/async.cljc`, `dao/jing/coordinate.cljc`,      | design lands.               |\\\\n793: |                            | `dao/space/dht.cljc`, `yin/repl.cljc`, `yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc` and the other            |                             |\\\\n794: |                            | `yang/python/antlr/*.cljc` with arms, `dao/stream/udp.cljc`, `dao/stream/journal.cljc`          |                             |\\\\n795: |                            | (`locking`), `dao/space/transactor.cljc`, `dao/space/schema.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc`  |                             |\\\\n796: |                            | (`locking`), and every remaining closure file whose arms are only `catch`/hint/protocol syntax  |                             |\\\\n797: |                            | is **not** on list 1 (it is exempt by pattern).                                                 |                             |\\\\n798: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\\\n799: \\\\n800: **Baseline versus additions and deletions.** The H0 baseline is the set of\\\\n801: **existing** files above (every entry except the planned additions named\\\\n802: in the profile row). The planned additions are the seven `dao/host/*.cljc`\\\\n803: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\\\\n804: three: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\\\\n805: JVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\\\\n806: Jing writer, a lane-specific file that the seams row excludes and the first\\\\n807: row lists, so that the lane-specific category cannot silently retain it).\\\\n808: The final list 1 after H4 is therefore: the baseline minus the first row\\\\n809: (except `sign.cljc` for `generate`), both deleted Jing writers included in\\\\n810: that subtraction, plus the seven profile files. The host-library gate of\\\\n811: §8.2 is consistent with it.\\\\n812: \\\\n813: ### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\\\\n814: \\\\n815: A literal `grep` over `src/cljc` is **not** the gate: it matches a docstring\\\\n816: in the untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` (\\\\\\\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\\\\\\\", V) and the\\\\n817: out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`:rgba8unorm`, V), so\\\\n818: its asserted result would be false. The gate is instead `dao.host.gate-test`\\\\n819: run in **library mode**, which **lands with H2**, not H0: H0 is a freeze\\\\n820: with no source change and the library mode has no consumer before H2's\\\\n821: deletion, so building it in H0 would add a deliverable nothing exercises\\\\n822: and nothing can falsify; H2 builds it with the H2 name list and its two\\\\n823: negative tests (below), and H3 extends the name list. In library mode the\\\\n824: gate takes the H0 closure tool's tagged file list\\\\n825: for the adopted closure (so out-of-scope files never count), reads each\\\\n826: file with the Clojure reader per lane feature (so comments and string\\\\n827: literals, docstrings included, never count), and collects symbols, class\\\\n828: names and import/require forms; a hit is any such symbol naming\\\\n829: `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`, `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm`\\\\n830: (H2) or `MessageDigest`, `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,\\\\n831: `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` (H3) in a file outside `dao/host/`\\\\n832: and, for H3's Ed25519 names, outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (`generate`,\\\\n833: deferred). Codec-track files stay on list 1 and are not scanned by this\\\\n834: mode (their arms are the codec track's). The gate fails distinctly when the\\\\n835: closure list is empty or a file cannot be read, which is a scan error, not\\\\n836: \\\\\\\"no hits\\\\\\\".\\\\n837: \\\\n838: ### 8.3 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\\\\n839: \\\\n840: Codec-track source files (`codec.md` §7.1): `dao/stream/ws.cljc`,\\\\n841: `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,\\\\n842: `remote_channel.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`, `data.cljc`, the four ws adapters,\\\\n843: `yin/repl/{serve,connect}.cljc`. Codec-track test namespaces (`codec.md`\\\\n844: §7.2): the 22 requiring Transit, including `ws_test`, `ws-codec-test`,\\\\n845: `remote-route-test`, `loopback-net`, `transit-test`, `dao.stream.cbor-test`,\\\\n846: `dao.jing.stream-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`.\\\\n847: \\\\n848: H0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\\\\n849: `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\\\\n850: `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,\\\\n851: `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\\\\n852: `yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\\\\n853: `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`,\\\\n854: `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc`, `dao/data/arrays.cljc`.\\\\n855: H0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\\\\n856: `yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\\\\n857: `dao/jing_test`, `yin/vm/linker/sign_test`, `dao/stream/base64_test`,\\\\n858: `yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\\\\n859: \\\\n860: Intersection: none, with two recorded deferrals: `dao/stream/codec.cljc:45`\\\\n861: (`host-bytes?` over `dao.host.bytes`) after C4, and `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`\\\\n862: (the transport writer) is **not** touched by H4. The `dao.stream.cbor-test`\\\\n863: and `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\\\\n864: (§9.1) would touch `ws.cljc:122`, `ws_test.cljc:11` and\\\\n865: `remote_route_test.cljc:24` (V: identity-less ring creation), which is why\\\\n866: it is deferred behind the codec track as well as behind its own design.\\\\n867: \\\\n868: Coordination with a host-lane probe track: its \\\\\\\"narrow source adaptations\\\\\\\"\\\\n869: (R: the spike touched `integer/host.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`,\\\\n870: `cbor/boring.cljc`) are exactly the H1-H4 files; under OQ3 that work is\\\\n871: paused until H4 lands and needs file-level coordination, not just a rebase.\\\\n872: \\\"}]}],\\\"meta\\\":{\\\"source\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"messageId\\\":\\\"6c32c1c1-f3e0-464e-9c58-38125c25fff6\\\"}},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thinking\\\",\\\"thinking\\\":\\\"Here I'll read the tools: closure.clj, gate_test.clj, corpus_hashes.clj. These are probably large. Main check items:\\\\n\\\\n(a) Fidelity of the closure tool: features per lane, resolution src/<lane> taking precedence over src/cljc, not treating :as-alias/string libspecs as dependencies, handling of #?@ (tools.namespace's read-ns-decl processes reader conditionals with the given features — splicing is also handled by the reader). Verify the strip-nils adaptation. Independency of the second traversal in gate_test: it must not share code with tools.namespace, and must use tools.reader's :preserve and its own arm selection.\\\\n\\\\n(b) Gate tests: in-memory negatives, scan-failure, exemption by form, honesty of list 1 (:h0-unlisted 16).\\\\n\\\\n(c) corpus_hashes: 18 files, tests assert the digests.\\\\n\\\\n(d) Verify F2 myself: grep for random-uuid occurrences within src/cljc; grep for places that require dao.await / yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.\\\\n\\\\n(e) Scope: only src/dev/host_boundary, test/dao/host/gate_test.clj, docs/design/host-boundary/* — confirm that deps.edn/bb.edn are unchanged (compared to base? Can't diff without git, but can compare the main tree's deps.edn with what I saw in j0c... the main tree's deps.edn was already read earlier in this session (j0c worktree + main). Check whether the host-h0 worktree's deps.edn matches main. Actually base eacaed90 is the local master; the main tree's deps.edn that I read in a previous turn — the worktree one should be identical. Quick check by grepping for hb alias (should not exist).\\\\n\\\\nRead closure.clj and gate_test.clj. gate_test is probably big (10 deftests + traversal B). First read closure.clj and corpus_hashes.clj, then gate_test.clj, after that do targeted greps.\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Now the tool sources.\\\\n\\\\n\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"call_a96da9c82ca34cc4a5ec9729\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_file\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj\\\",\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj\\\"]}}],\\\"meta\\\":{\\\"source\\\":\\\"model\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":1792522654730,\\\"messageId\\\":\\\"11461243-dd8b-40f3-8173-d080c8cddc9f\\\"}},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"call_a96da9c82ca34cc4a5ec9729\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Read 2/2 files\\\\n--- File Contents ---\\\\n\\\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (clojure)\\\\n(ns host-boundary.closure\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The adopted closure of dao.stream.host-boundary.md §3.1, per lane.\\\\n\\\\n   A require-form traversal from yin.repl.main over the ns declarations,\\\\n   parsed by clojure.tools.namespace.parse (read-ns-decl with the lane's\\\\n   reader features, deps-from-ns-decl for :require, :use and\\\\n   :require-macros; :as-alias and string (npm, dart:) libspecs are not\\\\n   dependencies). Lane features: :clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs},\\\\n   :cljd #{:cljd :clj} (the cljd build also reads :clj arms; the first\\\\n   matching arm wins, as in tools.reader). A namespace resolves to\\\\n   src/<lane>/<path>.<lane> first (the shadow: yin.repl.host is\\\\n   host.cljc on the JVM, host.cljs and host.cljd elsewhere), then\\\\n   src/cljc/<path>.cljc; a namespace with neither (clojure.core, a\\\\n   library) is outside the closure.\\\\n\\\\n   It is not a compiler-resolved call graph: it over-includes a namespace\\\\n   required but unused, and does not see dynamic loading.\\\\n\\\\n   Each file is tagged with its §3.1 classes (a set: a file can sit in\\\\n   several rows of the §3.1 table; :none means no host contact beyond the\\\\n   §3.3 exempt syntax).\\\\n\\\\n   Run from the repo root:\\\\n     clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                      :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace\\\\n                                   {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.5.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}}}}' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure [--check]\\\\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn and\\\\n   prints the totals; --check writes nothing and exits 1 when a committed\\\\n   file differs from the computed closure.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (:require\\\\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\\\\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\\\\n    [clojure.set :as set]\\\\n    [clojure.string :as str]\\\\n    [clojure.tools.namespace.parse :as parse]\\\\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def root 'yin.repl.main)\\\\n(def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\\\\n(def out-dir \\\\\\\"docs/design/host-boundary\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def lane-features\\\\n  {:clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs}, :cljd #{:cljd :clj}})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn ns->path\\\\n  [ns-sym]\\\\n  (-> (name ns-sym) (str/replace \\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"_\\\\\\\") (str/replace \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\")))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn resolve-file\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The repo-relative file for ns-sym on lane, or nil.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [lane ns-sym]\\\\n  (let [p (ns->path ns-sym)\\\\n        lane-dir (name lane)]\\\\n    (some (fn [f] (when (.isFile (io/file f)) f))\\\\n          [(str \\\\\\\"src/\\\\\\\" lane-dir \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\" p \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" lane-dir)\\\\n           (str \\\\\\\"src/cljc/\\\\\\\" p \\\\\\\".cljc\\\\\\\")])))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn strip-nils\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Drops the nil a lane's arm leaves in a libspec position\\\\n   (`#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` reads as nil on :cljd); deps-from-ns-decl\\\\n   refuses nil as unparsable, the compilers ignore it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [form]\\\\n  (walk/postwalk (fn [x]\\\\n                   (cond (vector? x) (vec (remove nil? x))\\\\n                         (seq? x) (apply list (remove nil? x))\\\\n                         :else x))\\\\n                 form))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn ns-decl\\\\n  [lane file]\\\\n  (with-open [r (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader file))]\\\\n    (strip-nils (parse/read-ns-decl r {:read-cond :allow\\\\n                                       :features (lane-features lane)}))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn lane-closure\\\\n  \\\\\\\"{file ns-sym} for every file reachable from root on lane.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [lane]\\\\n  (loop [todo [root]\\\\n         seen #{}\\\\n         files {}]\\\\n    (if-let [n (first todo)]\\\\n      (if (seen n)\\\\n        (recur (rest todo) seen files)\\\\n        (let [seen (conj seen n)]\\\\n          (if-let [f (resolve-file lane n)]\\\\n            (let [decl (ns-decl lane f)\\\\n                  deps (sort (parse/deps-from-ns-decl decl))]\\\\n              (when-not (= n (parse/name-from-ns-decl decl))\\\\n                (throw (ex-info \\\\\\\"ns name does not match its file\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                {:lane lane :ns n :file f\\\\n                                 :declared (parse/name-from-ns-decl decl)})))\\\\n              (recur (concat (rest todo) deps) seen (assoc files f n)))\\\\n            (recur (rest todo) seen files))))\\\\n      files)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n;; §3.1 classes. Keys are namespaces; a row's namespaces are named exactly as\\\\n;; the §3.1 table names them, expanded where the table abbreviates (\\\\\\\".datagram\\\\\\\"\\\\n;; = dao.stream.datagram, \\\\\\\"the seams\\\\\\\" = the lane-specific ws/datagram files).\\\\n;; Files of the §3.2 random-uuid/rand list carry :deferred-entropy.\\\\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n\\\\n(def class-rows\\\\n  [[:profile-internal-pure \\\\\\\"H1-H2 (writer H4)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[yin.vm.integer.host dao.jing.cbor dao.jing.cbor.boring dao.jing.cbor.cljd\\\\n      yin.vm.debruijn yin.vm.debruijn-code yin.vm.data yin.vm.values\\\\n      dao.stream.chunks dao.stream.base64 dao.jing.dht yin.vm.linker\\\\n      dao.stream.datagram dao.data.arrays]]\\\\n   [:profile-hash-sign \\\\\\\"H3\\\\\\\" '[dao.jing yin.vm.linker.sign]]\\\\n   [:consumer \\\\\\\"H2 (require change only)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[yin.vm yin.vm.engine yin.vm.values yin.vm.data yin.vm.integer]]\\\\n   [:external-stream-seam \\\\\\\"none (existing streams)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[dao.stream.ws dao.stream.datagram dao.stream.udp\\\\n      dao.stream.ws.jvm dao.stream.ws.node dao.stream.ws.dart\\\\n      dao.stream.ws.browser dao.stream.datagram.jvm dao.stream.datagram.node\\\\n      dao.stream.datagram.dart yin.repl.host yin.repl.host.jvm\\\\n      yin.repl.host.common]]\\\\n   [:deferred-storage \\\\\\\"deferred §9.2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[dao.jing.file dao.space.store.fs dao.space.store\\\\n      dao.stream.journal.file dao.data.btree.storage]]\\\\n   [:deferred-entropy \\\\\\\"deferred §9.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[dao.stream.ringbuffer dao.stream.memory-log dao.stream.ws\\\\n      dao.stream.remote dao.stream.remote-pair dao.stream.remote-route\\\\n      dao.stream.journal dao.jing.content.step dao.lease dao.await\\\\n      dao.space.store.fs yin.vm.linker yin.vm.ucf.custody\\\\n      yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve yin.vm.telemetry\\\\n      yin.repl yin.repl.dht dao.stream.rpc dao.jing.dht dao.space.dht\\\\n      yin.vm.linker.sign]]\\\\n   [:deferred-timers \\\\\\\"deferred §9.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[dao.jing.content.async dao.jing.coordinate dao.jing.content.driver\\\\n      dao.data.btree.storage]]\\\\n   [:driver \\\\\\\"driver (ambient reads deferred §9.1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[yin.repl.main yin.repl yin.repl.state]]\\\\n   [:deferred-stage \\\\\\\"deferred §9.3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[yang.antlr.cst yang.frontend yang.stage yin.repl.frontends]]\\\\n   [:deferred-gensym \\\\\\\"deferred §9.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[yang.clojure yang.php dao.space.transact]]\\\\n   [:runtime-prereq \\\\\\\"table C, no slice\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[dao.data.btree dao.jing.file dao.stream.journal dao.space.transactor\\\\n      dao.space.schema yin.vm.ucf.authority]]\\\\n   ;; §3.1 names transit, cbor and codec; the rest are the codec track's\\\\n   ;; files by §8.3 (and ws-project by §8.1's codec row) and the lane twins.\\\\n   [:codec-track \\\\\\\"codec track, untouched (§8.3)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    '[dao.stream.transit dao.stream.cbor dao.stream.codec\\\\n      dao.stream.cbor.boring dao.stream.cbor.cljd dao.stream.transit.cljd\\\\n      dao.stream.ws dao.stream.remote-channel dao.stream.ws-project\\\\n      dao.jing.stream dao.data dao.stream.ws.jvm dao.stream.ws.node\\\\n      dao.stream.ws.dart dao.stream.ws.browser yin.repl.serve\\\\n      yin.repl.connect]]\\\\n   [:internal-pure-display \\\\\\\"none (list 1, display only)\\\\\\\" '[dao.pretty]]])\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def prefix-rows\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Rows the §3.1 table names by prefix (`yang.python.antlr.*`).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [[:deferred-stage \\\\\\\"yang.python.antlr.\\\\\\\"]])\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def lane-rows\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Lane-specific files the §3.1 table does not name in a row but §3.1's\\\\n   lane-specific list and §8.1's \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Seams and driver\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" row place: the\\\\n   waitset timer drivers (setTimeout, Timer) are seams of dao.stream.waitset.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  '{dao.stream.waitset.driver #{:external-stream-seam}})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn classes-of\\\\n  [ns-sym]\\\\n  (let [s (name ns-sym)\\\\n        cs (into (set (keep (fn [[c _ nss]] (when (some #{ns-sym} nss) c))\\\\n                            class-rows))\\\\n                 (keep (fn [[c pre]] (when (str/starts-with? s pre) c))\\\\n                       prefix-rows))\\\\n        cs (into cs (lane-rows ns-sym))]\\\\n    (if (seq cs) cs #{:none})))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def class-legend\\\\n  (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [[c slice _]] [c slice]) class-rows)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn lane-report\\\\n  [lane files shared]\\\\n  {:lane lane\\\\n   :root root\\\\n   :features (lane-features lane)\\\\n   :total (count files)\\\\n   :shared (count shared)\\\\n   :lane-specific (count (remove shared (keys files)))\\\\n   :class-legend (assoc class-legend :none \\\\\\\"no host contact beyond §3.3\\\\\\\")\\\\n   :files (vec (for [[f n] (sort-by key files)]\\\\n                 {:file f\\\\n                  :ns n\\\\n                  :shared (contains? shared f)\\\\n                  :classes (into (sorted-set) (classes-of n))}))})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn compute\\\\n  []\\\\n  (let [closures (into {} (map (fn [l] [l (lane-closure l)]) lanes))\\\\n        shared (apply set/intersection (map (comp set keys) (vals closures)))]\\\\n    {:shared shared\\\\n     :reports (into {} (map (fn [[l fs]] [l (lane-report l fs shared)])\\\\n                            closures))}))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn render\\\\n  [report]\\\\n  (str \\\\\\\";; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (host-boundary H0).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n       \\\\\\\";; Do not edit by hand; regenerate with the command in that file's ns doc.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n       (with-out-str\\\\n         (binding [*print-namespace-maps* false]\\\\n           (pp/pprint report)))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn out-file\\\\n  [lane]\\\\n  (str out-dir \\\\\\\"/closure-\\\\\\\" (name lane) \\\\\\\".edn\\\\\\\"))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn -main\\\\n  [& args]\\\\n  (let [check? (some #{\\\\\\\"--check\\\\\\\"} args)\\\\n        {:keys [shared reports]} (compute)\\\\n        stale (atom [])]\\\\n    (doseq [l lanes]\\\\n      (let [r (reports l)\\\\n            text (render r)\\\\n            f (io/file (out-file l))]\\\\n        (println (format \\\\\\\"%-5s total %d shared %d lane-specific %d\\\\\\\"\\\\n                         (name l) (:total r) (:shared r) (:lane-specific r)))\\\\n        (if check?\\\\n          (when-not (and (.isFile f) (= text (slurp f)))\\\\n            (swap! stale conj (out-file l)))\\\\n          (do (io/make-parents f)\\\\n              (spit f text)))))\\\\n    (println \\\\\\\"shared (all three lanes):\\\\\\\" (count shared))\\\\n    (when (seq @stale)\\\\n      (println \\\\\\\"STALE:\\\\\\\" (str/join \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\" @stale))\\\\n      (System/exit 1))\\\\n    (shutdown-agents)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj (clojure)\\\\n(ns host-boundary.corpus-hashes\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The corpus hash set of dao.stream.host-boundary.md H0 (d): the SHA-256\\\\n   of every file under the Jing corpus (test/resources/dao/jing) and the\\\\n   codec wire fixtures (test/fixtures/codec), which H1-H4 must keep\\\\n   byte-identical.\\\\n\\\\n   Run from the repo root with babashka:\\\\n     bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj [--check]\\\\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn; --check writes\\\\n   nothing and exits 1 when a file's bytes, or the file set, differ from\\\\n   the committed hash set. dao.host.gate-test asserts the same on the JVM\\\\n   lane.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (:require\\\\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\\\\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\\\\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\\\\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def roots [\\\\\\\"test/resources/dao/jing\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"test/fixtures/codec\\\\\\\"])\\\\n(def out-file \\\\\\\"docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn sha-256\\\\n  [path]\\\\n  (let [d (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \\\\\\\"SHA-256\\\\\\\")]\\\\n    (apply str (map #(format \\\\\\\"%02x\\\\\\\" (bit-and % 0xff))\\\\n                    (.digest d (fs/read-all-bytes path))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn hash-set*\\\\n  []\\\\n  {:algorithm \\\\\\\"SHA-256\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :regenerate \\\\\\\"bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :roots roots\\\\n   :files (into (sorted-map)\\\\n                (for [r roots\\\\n                      p (fs/glob r \\\\\\\"**\\\\\\\")\\\\n                      :when (fs/regular-file? p)\\\\n                      :let [f (str/replace (str p) \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\")]]\\\\n                  [f (sha-256 p)]))})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn render\\\\n  [m]\\\\n  (str \\\\\\\";; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj (host-boundary H0).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n       \\\\\\\";; Do not edit by hand; H1-H4 keep these bytes identical.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n       (with-out-str (pp/pprint m))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn -main\\\\n  [& args]\\\\n  (let [m (hash-set*)\\\\n        text (render m)]\\\\n    (println (count (:files m)) \\\\\\\"files\\\\\\\")\\\\n    (if (some #{\\\\\\\"--check\\\\\\\"} args)\\\\n      (let [committed (when (fs/exists? out-file) (edn/read-string (slurp out-file)))]\\\\n        (if (= (:files committed) (:files m))\\\\n          (println \\\\\\\"corpus identical to\\\\\\\" out-file)\\\\n          (do (println \\\\\\\"CORPUS DIFFERS from\\\\\\\" out-file)\\\\n              (doseq [f (sort (into (set (keys (:files m))) (keys (:files committed))))\\\\n                      :when (not= (get (:files m) f) (get (:files committed) f))]\\\\n                (println \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\" f))\\\\n              (System/exit 1))))\\\\n      (spit out-file text))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \\\\\\\"babashka.file\\\\\\\"))\\\\n  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\\\\n\\\\n\\\"}]}],\\\"meta\\\":{\\\"source\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"messageId\\\":\\\"8f350e40-8203-4d56-8a4b-8e87838f5125\\\"}},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thinking\\\",\\\"thinking\\\":\\\"closure.clj looks fine: lane features are correct (:cljd #{:cljd :clj}), resolution order prioritizes lane and then cljc, tools.namespace's read-ns-decl and deps-from-ns-decl (:as-alias is handled by tools.namespace 1.5.0 — deps-from-ns-decl excludes :as-alias; string libspecs: deps-from-ns-decl maps symbols; strings are… actually deps-from-ns-decl in 1.5.0 only returns symbols; string libspecs like \\\\\\\"npm:foo\\\\\\\" are ignored? The docstring claims they aren't dependencies — tools.namespace's parse-deps… in 1.5.0 does `deps-from-ns-decl` return only symbols? I think the map-spec parsing takes the first element that's a symbol; string libspecs are skipped (there was a fix to ignore strings). Reasonable; also the cljd lane reads string libspecs for `dart:` packages. ns name mismatch check → throw (fail-closed). #?@ inside ns forms: tools.reader's read-cond :allow natively handles splicing ✓ (r3's flaw was a homegrown regex script; the new tool delegates to the reader). strip-nils for cases like `#?(:cljd nil :clj [...])` → nil libspecs. Sound adaptation.\\\\n\\\\nPotential under-inclusion risks: (1) ns forms that fail to parse → read-ns-decl throws → tool fails loudly (fail-closed, not silent). (2) `:use` is included ✓. (3) Dynamic requires not visible — disclosed. (4) resolve-file: only checks src/<lane> and src/cljc — namespaces that exist only in src/clj but are also needed for cljs? For the cljs lane, yin.repl.host resolves to src/cljs/..., then src/cljc; src/clj is not included in cljs resolution — correct per lane semantics (shadow uses src/cljs + src/cljc). For the cljd lane: src/cljd, then src/cljc — but cljd also reads :clj arms; could a namespace exist only in src/clj and be required from cljd? If so, resolution fails → silently excluded from the closure! Hmm: the resolve-file for lane cljd checks \\\\\\\"src/cljd/...\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"src/cljc/...\\\\\\\". If a file exists only in src/clj and is reachable via a :clj arm on the cljd lane, it gets silently dropped. Does the cljd classpath include src/clj? The deps.edn :clojuredart build… the repo's cljd compile uses paths src/clj src/cljc src/cljd (root :paths includes everything). In practice, ClojureDart's resolution includes src/clj. But §3.1's methodology says \\\\\\\"resolve each namespace first to a file under src/<lane>, then to src/cljc\\\\\\\" — the design itself specifies this two-root rule, so the tool is faithful to the design. If src/clj-only namespaces were reachable from cljd, the design's totals wouldn't match either. Not a flaw relative to the spec; but worth mentioning? The design explicitly states this rule and the totals agree at 142/140/141, and traversal B independently agrees. OK.\\\\n\\\\n(5) Traversal B in gate_test — need to read gate_test.clj to verify independence and gate logic. Probably a large file. Let's read it.\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Now the gate test — the biggest adversarial target.\\\\n\\\\n\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"call_2cad5919095c4bbca7a595f2\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_file\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\\\"}}],\\\"meta\\\":{\\\"source\\\":\\\"model\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":1792522691294,\\\"messageId\\\":\\\"5801e7e8-8738-4dff-ad44-9af381d64d22\\\"}},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"call_2cad5919095c4bbca7a595f2\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Read 1/1 file, 772 lines\\\\n1: (ns dao.host.gate-test\\\\n2:   \\\\\\\"The H0 freeze gate of docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (§8 H0,\\\\n3:    §8.1, §3.2, §3.3), over the adopted closure committed by\\\\n4:    src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj under docs/design/host-boundary/.\\\\n5: \\\\n6:    The gate reads every closure file with tools.reader (:read-cond\\\\n7:    :preserve, so every lane's arms are seen; comments, strings and\\\\n8:    docstrings never count) and fails when\\\\n9:    - a file outside list 1 holds a non-exempt host arm (§3.3 exempts:\\\\n10:      ns-form arms, catch-type arms, arms equal but for hints, protocol\\\\n11:      blocks directly inside deftype/defrecord/reify/extend bodies,\\\\n12:      print-method defmethods, exists? tests, (Object.)/(js-obj)\\\\n13:      sentinels); a lane-specific file (.clj .cljs .cljd) is a host arm as\\\\n14:      a whole;\\\\n15:    - a file holds more resolved effect calls of a kind than list 2\\\\n16:      permits (the §3.2 kinds, and calls of the §2.4 M entries).\\\\n17:    Effect calls are resolved lexically: a symbol bound by let, fn, loop,\\\\n18:    for, doseq, catch, letfn or a deftype method, defined in its file, or\\\\n19:    excluded by :refer-clojure, is not the core function; quoted forms and\\\\n20:    (comment ...) are data. Reading zero files, or failing to read one, is\\\\n21:    a scan failure, distinct from a pass.\\\\n22: \\\\n23:    JVM lane only: the gate reads source text from disk; what it checks is\\\\n24:    the same text on every lane.\\\\n25: \\\\n26:    Also here: the independent second traversal of the closure (a\\\\n27:    reader-form walker that selects reader-conditional arms itself and\\\\n28:    parses libspecs itself, sharing no code with tools.namespace), which\\\\n29:    must agree with the committed closure files.\\\\\\\"\\\\n30:   (:require\\\\n31:     [clojure.edn :as edn]\\\\n32:     [clojure.java.io :as io]\\\\n33:     [clojure.set :as set]\\\\n34:     [clojure.string :as str]\\\\n35:     [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\n36:     [clojure.tools.reader :as reader]\\\\n37:     [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt])\\\\n38:   (:import\\\\n39:     (clojure.lang\\\\n40:       ReaderConditional)))\\\\n41: \\\\n42: \\\\n43: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n44: ;; Reading\\\\n45: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n46: \\\\n47: (defn read-forms\\\\n48:   \\\\\\\"Every top-level form of text, reader conditionals preserved.\\\\\\\"\\\\n49:   [text]\\\\n50:   (binding [reader/*read-eval* false\\\\n51:             ;; ::alias/kw needs no real namespace: keywords never count\\\\n52:             reader/*alias-map* (fn [sym] sym)\\\\n53:             reader/*default-data-reader-fn* (fn [tag v] (tagged-literal tag v))]\\\\n54:     (let [rdr (rt/indexing-push-back-reader text 1)]\\\\n55:       (loop [acc []]\\\\n56:         (let [form (reader/read {:read-cond :preserve :eof ::eof} rdr)]\\\\n57:           (if (= ::eof form) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\\\\n58: \\\\n59: \\\\n60: (defn rc?\\\\n61:   [x]\\\\n62:   (instance? ReaderConditional x))\\\\n63: \\\\n64: \\\\n65: (defn rc-arms\\\\n66:   \\\\\\\"[[feature form] ...] of a reader conditional.\\\\\\\"\\\\n67:   [^ReaderConditional rc]\\\\n68:   (map vec (partition 2 (.-form rc))))\\\\n69: \\\\n70: \\\\n71: (defn splicing?\\\\n72:   [^ReaderConditional rc]\\\\n73:   (boolean (.-splicing rc)))\\\\n74: \\\\n75: \\\\n76: (defn head\\\\n77:   [x]\\\\n78:   (when (and (seq? x) (symbol? (first x))) (first x)))\\\\n79: \\\\n80: \\\\n81: (defn line-of\\\\n82:   [x]\\\\n83:   (:line (meta x)))\\\\n84: \\\\n85: \\\\n86: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n87: ;; The independent closure traversal (traversal B)\\\\n88: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n89: \\\\n90: (def closure-root 'yin.repl.main)\\\\n91: (def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\\\\n92: (def lane-features {:clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs}, :cljd #{:cljd :clj}})\\\\n93: \\\\n94: \\\\n95: (defn select-arms\\\\n96:   \\\\\\\"form with every reader conditional replaced by its lane arm: the first\\\\n97:    arm whose feature is in features or is :default; a splicing arm's\\\\n98:    elements spliced into the enclosing collection; no arm, nothing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n99:   [features form]\\\\n100:   (let [pick (fn [rc]\\\\n101:                (some (fn [[k v]] (when (or (features k) (= :default k)) [v]))\\\\n102:                      (rc-arms rc)))\\\\n103:         expand (fn [xs]\\\\n104:                  (mapcat (fn [x]\\\\n105:                            (if (rc? x)\\\\n106:                              (when-let [[v] (pick x)]\\\\n107:                                (if (splicing? x)\\\\n108:                                  (map #(select-arms features %) v)\\\\n109:                                  [(select-arms features v)]))\\\\n110:                              [(select-arms features x)]))\\\\n111:                          xs))]\\\\n112:     (cond\\\\n113:       (rc? form) (some->> (pick form) first (select-arms features))\\\\n114:       (seq? form) (apply list (expand form))\\\\n115:       (vector? form) (vec (expand form))\\\\n116:       (map? form) (into {} (map vec (partition 2 (expand (mapcat identity form)))))\\\\n117:       :else form)))\\\\n118: \\\\n119: \\\\n120: (defn libspec-deps\\\\n121:   [spec]\\\\n122:   (cond\\\\n123:     (symbol? spec) [spec]\\\\n124:     (or (string? spec) (keyword? spec) (nil? spec)) []\\\\n125:     (sequential? spec)\\\\n126:     (let [[a b] spec\\\\n127:           opts (rest spec)]\\\\n128:       (cond\\\\n129:         (string? a) []\\\\n130:         (and (symbol? a) (or (nil? b) (keyword? b)))\\\\n131:         (if (and (= :as-alias b) (not-any? #{:as :refer :refer-macros :include-macros} opts))\\\\n132:           []\\\\n133:           [a])\\\\n134:         (symbol? a)\\\\n135:         (mapcat (fn [s]\\\\n136:                   (map #(symbol (str a \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" %)) (libspec-deps s)))\\\\n137:                 (remove nil? (rest spec)))\\\\n138:         :else []))\\\\n139:     :else []))\\\\n140: \\\\n141: \\\\n142: (defn ns-deps\\\\n143:   \\\\\\\"The namespaces an ns form requires on a lane: :require, :use and\\\\n144:    :require-macros clauses.\\\\\\\"\\\\n145:   [features ns-form]\\\\n146:   (let [f (select-arms features ns-form)]\\\\n147:     (->> (rest f)\\\\n148:          (filter seq?)\\\\n149:          (filter #(#{:require :use :require-macros} (first %)))\\\\n150:          (mapcat rest)\\\\n151:          (mapcat libspec-deps)\\\\n152:          set)))\\\\n153: \\\\n154: \\\\n155: (defn lane-file\\\\n156:   [lane ns-sym]\\\\n157:   (let [p (-> (name ns-sym) (str/replace \\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"_\\\\\\\") (str/replace \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"))]\\\\n158:     (some #(when (.isFile (io/file %)) %)\\\\n159:           [(str \\\\\\\"src/\\\\\\\" (name lane) \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\" p \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" (name lane))\\\\n160:            (str \\\\\\\"src/cljc/\\\\\\\" p \\\\\\\".cljc\\\\\\\")])))\\\\n161: \\\\n162: \\\\n163: (defn traverse\\\\n164:   \\\\\\\"The closure files of lane from closure-root, by traversal B.\\\\\\\"\\\\n165:   [lane]\\\\n166:   (loop [todo [closure-root] seen #{} files #{}]\\\\n167:     (if-let [n (first todo)]\\\\n168:       (if (seen n)\\\\n169:         (recur (rest todo) seen files)\\\\n170:         (if-let [f (lane-file lane n)]\\\\n171:           (let [ns-form (first (filter #(= 'ns (head %)) (read-forms (slurp f))))]\\\\n172:             (recur (concat (rest todo) (sort (ns-deps (lane-features lane) ns-form)))\\\\n173:                    (conj seen n)\\\\n174:                    (conj files f)))\\\\n175:           (recur (rest todo) (conj seen n) files)))\\\\n176:       files)))\\\\n177: \\\\n178: \\\\n179: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n180: ;; The committed closure (traversal A, src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj)\\\\n181: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n182: \\\\n183: (defn committed-closure\\\\n184:   [lane]\\\\n185:   (edn/read-string (slurp (str \\\\\\\"docs/design/host-boundary/closure-\\\\\\\" (name lane) \\\\\\\".edn\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n186: \\\\n187: \\\\n188: (defn closure-files\\\\n189:   \\\\\\\"The union of the three lanes' committed closure files.\\\\\\\"\\\\n190:   []\\\\n191:   (into (sorted-set) (mapcat #(map :file (:files (committed-closure %))) lanes)))\\\\n192: \\\\n193: \\\\n194: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n195: ;; Host arms (§3.3 exemptions)\\\\n196: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n197: \\\\n198: (def deftype-heads\\\\n199:   '#{deftype defrecord reify extend-type extend-protocol specify specify!})\\\\n200: \\\\n201: \\\\n202: (def sentinels\\\\n203:   '#{(Object.) (js-obj) (js/Object.) (java.lang.Object.)})\\\\n204: \\\\n205: \\\\n206: (defn exemption\\\\n207:   \\\\\\\"The §3.3 pattern that exempts rc, given its ancestors (outermost first),\\\\n208:    or nil.\\\\\\\"\\\\n209:   [rc ancestors]\\\\n210:   (let [parent (peek ancestors)\\\\n211:         arms (map second (rc-arms rc))\\\\n212:         catch-form? #(and (seq? %) (= 'catch (first %)))]\\\\n213:     (cond\\\\n214:       (some #(= 'ns (head %)) ancestors) :ns-require-arm\\\\n215:       (and (catch-form? parent) (identical? rc (second parent))) :catch-type\\\\n216:       (and (< 1 (count arms)) (apply = arms)) :hint-only\\\\n217:       (and (splicing? rc) (deftype-heads (head parent))) :protocol-block\\\\n218:       (some #(and (= 'defmethod (head %)) (= 'print-method (second %))) ancestors) :print-method\\\\n219:       (every? #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmethod (first %)) (= 'print-method (second %))) arms)\\\\n220:       :print-method\\\\n221:       (every? #(= 'exists? (head %)) arms) :exists\\\\n222:       (every? sentinels arms) :sentinel\\\\n223:       :else nil)))\\\\n224: \\\\n225: \\\\n226: (defn non-exempt-arms\\\\n227:   \\\\\\\"[line ...] of the non-exempt reader conditionals in forms.\\\\\\\"\\\\n228:   [forms]\\\\n229:   (let [acc (atom [])\\\\n230:         walk (fn walk\\\\n231:                [form ancestors]\\\\n232:                (let [down (conj ancestors form)]\\\\n233:                  (cond\\\\n234:                    (rc? form)\\\\n235:                    (do (when-not (exemption form ancestors)\\\\n236:                          (swap! acc conj (or (some (comp line-of second) (rc-arms form))\\\\n237:                                              (some line-of (rseq ancestors)))))\\\\n238:                        (doseq [[_ arm] (rc-arms form)]\\\\n239:                          (if (splicing? form)\\\\n240:                            (doseq [x arm] (walk x down))\\\\n241:                            (walk arm down))))\\\\n242:                    (and (seq? form) (= 'comment (first form))) nil\\\\n243:                    (map? form) (doseq [[k v] form] (walk k down) (walk v down))\\\\n244:                    (coll? form) (doseq [x form] (walk x down))\\\\n245:                    :else nil)))]\\\\n246:     (doseq [f forms] (walk f []))\\\\n247:     @acc))\\\\n248: \\\\n249: \\\\n250: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n251: ;; Resolved effect calls (§3.2 kinds, §2.4 M entries)\\\\n252: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n253: \\\\n254: (def core-ns #{nil \\\\\\\"clojure.core\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"cljs.core\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"cljd.core\\\\\\\"})\\\\n255: \\\\n256: \\\\n257: (defn effect-kind\\\\n258:   \\\\\\\"The §3.2 kind of a symbol that names a host effect, or nil. core? is\\\\n259:    false when an unqualified name is shadowed in its file.\\\\\\\"\\\\n260:   [sym core?]\\\\n261:   (let [n (name sym)\\\\n262:         q (namespace sym)\\\\n263:         core (and (contains? core-ns q) (or q core?))]\\\\n264:     (cond\\\\n265:       (and core (= n \\\\\\\"random-uuid\\\\\\\")) :random-uuid\\\\n266:       (and core (#{\\\\\\\"rand\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"rand-int\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"rand-nth\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"shuffle\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"random-sample\\\\\\\"} n)) :rand\\\\n267:       (or (str/includes? n \\\\\\\"SecureRandom\\\\\\\")\\\\n268:           (= n \\\\\\\"Random.secure\\\\\\\")\\\\n269:           (= n \\\\\\\"randomUUID\\\\\\\")\\\\n270:           (and (= q \\\\\\\"js\\\\\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"crypto\\\\\\\"))\\\\n271:           (#{\\\\\\\"getRandomValues\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"randomBytes\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"generateKey\\\\\\\"} n)) :secure-random\\\\n272:       (and core (= n \\\\\\\"gensym\\\\\\\")) :gensym\\\\n273:       (or (and (#{\\\\\\\"System\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"java.lang.System\\\\\\\"} q) (#{\\\\\\\"currentTimeMillis\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"nanoTime\\\\\\\"} n))\\\\n274:           (and (= q \\\\\\\"js\\\\\\\") (or (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"Date\\\\\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"performance\\\\\\\")))\\\\n275:           (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"DateTime.now\\\\\\\")\\\\n276:           (and q (str/ends-with? q \\\\\\\"Instant\\\\\\\") (= n \\\\\\\"now\\\\\\\"))) :clock\\\\n277:       (or (and (#{\\\\\\\"System\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"java.lang.System\\\\\\\"} q) (#{\\\\\\\"getenv\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"getProperty\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"getProperties\\\\\\\"} n))\\\\n278:           (and (= q \\\\\\\"js\\\\\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"process\\\\\\\"))\\\\n279:           (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"Platform.\\\\\\\")) :ambient\\\\n280:       (or (and core (#{\\\\\\\"println\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"print\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"prn\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"pr\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"printf\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"newline\\\\\\\"} n))\\\\n281:           (and (= q \\\\\\\"js\\\\\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"console\\\\\\\"))) :print\\\\n282:       (or (and (= q \\\\\\\"js\\\\\\\") (#{\\\\\\\"setTimeout\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"setInterval\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"setImmediate\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"queueMicrotask\\\\\\\"} n))\\\\n283:           (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"Timer\\\\\\\")\\\\n284:           (and (#{\\\\\\\"Thread\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"java.lang.Thread\\\\\\\"} q) (= n \\\\\\\"sleep\\\\\\\"))\\\\n285:           (str/starts-with? n \\\\\\\"Future.delayed\\\\\\\")) :timer\\\\n286:       :else nil)))\\\\n287: \\\\n288: \\\\n289: (def m-entry-nss\\\\n290:   \\\\\\\"The namespaces holding §2.4's M entries, now and after H1.\\\\\\\"\\\\n291:   '#{dao.data.arrays dao.host.bytes})\\\\n292: \\\\n293: \\\\n294: (def m-entry-names #{\\\\\\\"aset\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"acopy\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"asort\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"set!\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"copy!\\\\\\\"})\\\\n295: \\\\n296: \\\\n297: (defn all-arms\\\\n298:   \\\\\\\"form with every reader conditional replaced by all its arms, so every\\\\n299:    lane's text is seen: a splicing conditional's elements are spliced into\\\\n300:    the enclosing collection; a non-splicing one becomes (do arm ...), or,\\\\n301:    with splice-all?, is spliced too (for ns clauses, where position does\\\\n302:    not bind).\\\\\\\"\\\\n303:   ([form] (all-arms false form))\\\\n304:   ([splice-all? form]\\\\n305:    (let [expand (fn [xs]\\\\n306:                   (mapcat (fn [x]\\\\n307:                             (if (and (rc? x) (or splice-all? (splicing? x)))\\\\n308:                               (map #(all-arms splice-all? %)\\\\n309:                                    (mapcat (fn [[_ v]] (if (splicing? x) v [v])) (rc-arms x)))\\\\n310:                               [(all-arms splice-all? x)]))\\\\n311:                           xs))]\\\\n312:      (cond\\\\n313:        (rc? form) (cons 'do (map #(all-arms splice-all? %)\\\\n314:                                  (mapcat (fn [[_ v]] (if (splicing? form) v [v]))\\\\n315:                                          (rc-arms form))))\\\\n316:        (seq? form) (with-meta (apply list (expand form)) (meta form))\\\\n317:        (vector? form) (vec (expand form))\\\\n318:        (map? form) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(all-arms splice-all? k) (all-arms splice-all? v)])\\\\n319:                                  form))\\\\n320:        :else form))))\\\\n321: \\\\n322: \\\\n323: (defn file-scope\\\\n324:   \\\\\\\"{:aliases {alias ns} :refers {sym ns} :shadowed #{sym}} of a file:\\\\n325:    every lane's ns arms, its top-level defs, its :refer-clojure excludes.\\\\\\\"\\\\n326:   [forms]\\\\n327:   (let [ns-form (all-arms true (first (filter #(= 'ns (head %)) forms)))\\\\n328:         specs (->> (rest ns-form)\\\\n329:                    (filter seq?)\\\\n330:                    (filter #(#{:require :use} (first %)))\\\\n331:                    (mapcat rest)\\\\n332:                    (filter vector?))\\\\n333:         opts (fn [spec] (apply hash-map (rest (if (even? (count spec)) (butlast spec) spec))))\\\\n334:         excluded (->> (rest ns-form)\\\\n335:                       (filter #(and (seq? %) (= :refer-clojure (first %))))\\\\n336:                       (mapcat #(:exclude (apply hash-map (rest %)))))\\\\n337:         defs (->> forms\\\\n338:                   (map all-arms)\\\\n339:                   (mapcat (fn [f] (if (= 'do (head f)) (rest f) [f])))\\\\n340:                   (keep (fn [f]\\\\n341:                           (when (#{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro 'defonce 'declare\\\\n342:                                    'defprotocol 'defmulti} (head f))\\\\n343:                             (second f)))))]\\\\n344:     {:aliases (into {} (keep (fn [s] (when-let [a (:as (opts s))] [a (first s)])) specs))\\\\n345:      :refers (into {} (mapcat (fn [s]\\\\n346:                                 (let [r (:refer (opts s))]\\\\n347:                                   (when (sequential? r) (map (fn [x] [x (first s)]) r))))\\\\n348:                               specs))\\\\n349:      :shadowed (set (filter symbol? (concat excluded defs)))}))\\\\n350: \\\\n351: \\\\n352: (defn binding-syms\\\\n353:   \\\\\\\"Every symbol in a binding form (destructuring included).\\\\\\\"\\\\n354:   [b]\\\\n355:   (cond\\\\n356:     (symbol? b) (if (= '& b) [] [b])\\\\n357:     (map? b) (mapcat binding-syms (concat (keys b) (vals b)))\\\\n358:     (coll? b) (mapcat binding-syms b)\\\\n359:     :else []))\\\\n360: \\\\n361: \\\\n362: (def let-heads\\\\n363:   '#{let let* loop loop* when-let if-let when-some if-some when-first\\\\n364:      with-open dotimes for doseq})\\\\n365: \\\\n366: \\\\n367: (def fn-heads '#{fn fn* defn defn- defmacro defmethod})\\\\n368: \\\\n369: \\\\n370: (defn effect-calls\\\\n371:   \\\\\\\"[[kind line] ...] for the resolved effect calls in forms.\\\\\\\"\\\\n372:   [forms]\\\\n373:   (let [{:keys [aliases refers shadowed]} (file-scope forms)\\\\n374:         acc (atom [])\\\\n375:         hit! (fn [kind sym] (swap! acc conj [kind (line-of sym)]))\\\\n376:         resolve-m (fn [sym]\\\\n377:                     (if-let [q (namespace sym)]\\\\n378:                       (get aliases (symbol q) (symbol q))\\\\n379:                       (get refers sym)))]\\\\n380:     (letfn [(walk\\\\n381:               [form bound]\\\\n382:               (cond\\\\n383:                 (symbol? form)\\\\n384:                 (when-not (and (nil? (namespace form)) (bound form))\\\\n385:                   (if-let [k (effect-kind form (not (shadowed form)))]\\\\n386:                     (hit! k form)\\\\n387:                     (when (and (m-entry-nss (resolve-m form)) (m-entry-names (name form)))\\\\n388:                       (hit! :m-entry form))))\\\\n389: \\\\n390:                 (seq? form)\\\\n391:                 (let [h (head form)]\\\\n392:                   (cond\\\\n393:                     (#{'quote 'comment 'ns} h) nil\\\\n394:                     (let-heads h) (walk-let (second form) (nnext form) bound)\\\\n395:                     (= 'letfn h) (let [fns (second form)\\\\n396:                                        b (into bound (map first fns))]\\\\n397:                                    (doseq [f fns] (walk-fn (rest f) b))\\\\n398:                                    (walk-all (nnext form) b))\\\\n399:                     (fn-heads h) (walk-fn (rest form) bound)\\\\n400:                     (= 'catch h) (walk-all (drop 3 form) (conj bound (nth form 2 nil)))\\\\n401:                     (deftype-heads h) (let [fields (filter vector? (take 3 form))\\\\n402:                                             b (into bound (mapcat binding-syms fields))]\\\\n403:                                         (doseq [x (drop 2 form)]\\\\n404:                                           (if (and (seq? x) (vector? (second x)))\\\\n405:                                             (walk-fn x b)\\\\n406:                                             (walk x b))))\\\\n407:                     :else (walk-all form bound)))\\\\n408: \\\\n409:                 (map? form) (doseq [[k v] form] (walk k bound) (walk v bound))\\\\n410:                 (coll? form) (walk-all form bound)\\\\n411:                 :else nil))\\\\n412:             (walk-all [xs bound] (doseq [x xs] (walk x bound)))\\\\n413:             (walk-let\\\\n414:               [bvec body bound]\\\\n415:               (let [b (reduce (fn [b [lhs rhs]]\\\\n416:                                 (case lhs\\\\n417:                                   :let (do (walk-let rhs nil b) (into b (binding-syms (take-nth 2 rhs))))\\\\n418:                                   (:when :while) (do (walk rhs b) b)\\\\n419:                                   (do (walk rhs b) (into b (binding-syms lhs)))))\\\\n420:                               bound\\\\n421:                               (partition 2 (if (vector? bvec) bvec [])))]\\\\n422:                 (walk-all body b)))\\\\n423:             (walk-fn\\\\n424:               [tail bound]\\\\n425:               ;; tail: [name? doc? attrs? params body...] or [name? (params body...)...]\\\\n426:               (let [params (concat (filter vector? tail)\\\\n427:                                    (keep #(when (and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) (first %)) tail))\\\\n428:                     b (into (into bound (filter symbol? (take 1 tail)))\\\\n429:                             (mapcat binding-syms params))]\\\\n430:                 (walk-all (remove #(or (vector? %) (symbol? %)\\\\n431:                                        (and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))))\\\\n432:                                   tail)\\\\n433:                           b)\\\\n434:                 (doseq [x tail :when (and (seq? x) (vector? (first x)))]\\\\n435:                   (walk-all (rest x) b))))]\\\\n436:       (doseq [f forms] (walk (all-arms f) #{})))\\\\n437:     @acc))\\\\n438: \\\\n439: \\\\n440: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n441: ;; List 1 and list 2\\\\n442: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n443: \\\\n444: (def list-1\\\\n445:   \\\\\\\"The closure files permitted non-exempt host arms (§8.1), by category.\\\\n446:    Generated from the H0 tree by the gate and reconciled against the §8.1\\\\n447:    baseline; :h0-unlisted marks the files with real arms that §8.1 does\\\\n448:    not name (an H0 finding, to resolve before H1).\\\\\\\"\\\\n449:   {;; H1-H4 migration sources\\\\n450:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n451:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n452:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n453:    \\\\\\\"src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n454:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n455:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n456:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n457:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n458:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n459:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n460:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/chunks.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n461:    \\\\\\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/base64.cljc\\\\\\\" :migration-source\\\\n4