 path->ns\\n162:(defn convention-test-paths\\n170:(defn mentions?\\n301:(defn- ns-graph\\n458:    :cljs (#{\\\"cljs\\\" \\\"cljc\\\"} ext)\\n460:    :cljd (re-find #\\\"_test\\\\.clj[cd]$\\\" path)))\\n463:(defn lane-tests\\n474:(defn ns-regexp\\n494:  (if (= :cljd lane)\\n527:(defn serialized-pairs\\n532:  (if (and (seq (:clj selected)) (seq (:cljd selected))\\n535:    #{[:clj :cljd]}\\n683:     :cljs [\\\"clj\\\" \\\"-M:cljs\\\" \\\"-m\\\" \\\"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\\\" \\\"compile\\\" \\\"test\\\"\\n685:     :cljd [\\\"bb\\\" \\\"src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\\\" \\\"--only\\\" (str/join \\\",\\\" nses)])))\\n700:               (and (not slow?) (= :cljs lane)) (dissoc \\\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\\\"))\\n801:                serial (serialized-pairs index run)]\\n857:                serial (serialized-pairs index run)]\\n   350\\tunder the 5 s cut (the Python e2e per-test floor is about 2 to 3 s), not shared setup.\\n   351\\tA lower cut would shrink the quick tier further and move more tests to the slow tier.\\n   352\\t\\n   353\\t**How the per-test times were measured.** To time every deftest of a namespace alone,\\n   354\\trun it without the test runner's alias main (the `:test` alias's `-m cognitect.test-runner`\\n   355\\totherwise swallows `-e`, and every JVM runs the whole suite):\\n   356\\t\\n   357\\t```sh\\n   358\\tNS=<namespace> clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]}}}' -M:t timing.clj\\n   359\\t# timing.clj: require the namespace, for each deftest var that is not ^:slow:\\n   360\\t#   (binding [clojure.test/*test-out* (java.io.StringWriter.)] (clojure.test/test-vars [v]))\\n   361\\t# and print the elapsed nanoseconds. One-off setup (a `use-fixtures :once` or a parser\\n   362\\t# load) is paid by the first test in file order; check before tagging that test alone.\\n   363\\t```\\n   364\\t\\n   365\\t**Sharding the JVM lane by subsystem** (the quick tier; run on a server, see below). The\\n   366\\tshards come from `bb test:sub:list <subsystem>` for the 13 subsystems that hold JVM\\n   367\\ttests, so each subsystem is one JVM; the script also checks that the shards cover every\\n   368\\tJVM test namespace under `test/`:\\n   369\\t\\n   370\\t```sh\\n   371\\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n   372\\t# Usage: shard-jvm.sh <clone> [parallel]  -- JVM lane sharded by subsystem (fast tests, -e :slow)\\n   373\\tset -u\\n   374\\texport PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\\\"\\n   375\\tcd \\\"$1\\\" || exit 2\\n   376\\tPAR=\\\"${2:-8}\\\"\\n   377\\tmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\\n   378\\teval \\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\"\\n   379\\tOUT=\\\"$1/target-ci/shards\\\"; rm -rf \\\"$OUT\\\"; mkdir -p \\\"$OUT\\\"\\n   380\\tts() { date +%H:%M:%S; }\\n   381\\techo \\\"start $(ts) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) par=$PAR\\\" | tee \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   382\\tnpm ci --silent >\\\"$OUT/npm.log\\\" 2>&1                   && echo \\\"npm ok $(ts)\\\" | tee -a \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   383\\tbb build:yin-repl-node >\\\"$OUT/build-node.log\\\" 2>&1     && echo \\\"node repl built $(ts)\\\" | tee -a \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   384\\tbb gen:antlr >\\\"$OUT/antlr.log\\\" 2>&1             && echo \\\"antlr ok $(ts)\\\" | tee -a \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   385\\tSUBS=\\\"yang.python yin.repl yin.vm yin.vm.ucf dao.stream dao.jing dao.gui dao.space demo dao.data dao.postgraphics yang.base dao.base\\\"\\n   386\\t: > \\\"$OUT/covered.txt\\\"\\n   387\\tfor s in $SUBS; do\\n   388\\t  bb test:sub:list \\\"$s\\\" 2>/dev/null | awk \\\"/^clj:/{f=1;next} /^[A-Za-z]/{f=0} f{gsub(/ /,\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\");print}\\\" > \\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\"\\n   389\\t  cat \\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\" >> \\\"$OUT/covered.txt\\\"\\n   390\\t  echo \\\"$s $(wc -l < \\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\")\\\" >> \\\"$OUT/plan.txt\\\"\\n   391\\tdone\\n   392\\t# coverage: every JVM test namespace under test/ vs the union of the shards\\n   393\\tfind test -type f \\\\( -name \\\"*_test.clj\\\" -o -name \\\"*_test.cljc\\\" \\\\) | sed -e \\\"s#^test/##\\\" -e \\\"s#\\\\.cljc\\\\?\\\\$##\\\" -e \\\"s#/#.#g\\\" -e \\\"s#_#-#g\\\" | sort -u > \\\"$OUT/all.txt\\\"\\n   394\\tsort -u \\\"$OUT/covered.txt\\\" > \\\"$OUT/covered.sorted\\\"\\n   395\\tcomm -23 \\\"$OUT/all.txt\\\" \\\"$OUT/covered.sorted\\\" > \\\"$OUT/ns-uncovered.txt\\\"\\n   396\\techo \\\"all=$(wc -l < $OUT/all.txt) covered=$(wc -l < $OUT/covered.sorted) uncovered=$(wc -l < $OUT/ns-uncovered.txt)\\\" | tee -a \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   397\\trun_shard() {\\n   398\\t  s=$1; f=\\\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\\\"; [ -s \\\"$f\\\" ] || return 0\\n   399\\t  args=(); while read -r n; do args+=(-n \\\"$n\\\"); done < \\\"$f\\\"\\n   400\\t  t0=$(date +%s); clojure -M:test -e :slow \\\"${args[@]}\\\" >\\\"$OUT/$s.log\\\" 2>&1; rc=$?\\n   401\\t  echo \\\"$s rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-t0 )) $(ts) $(grep -E \\\"^Ran \\\" \\\"$OUT/$s.log\\\" | tail -1)\\\" | tee -a \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   402\\t}\\n   403\\texport -f run_shard; export OUT; export -f ts\\n   404\\tprintf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" $SUBS uncovered | xargs -P \\\"$PAR\\\" -I{} bash -c \\\"run_shard {}\\\"\\n   405\\techo \\\"done $(ts)\\\" | tee -a \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   406\\t```\\n   407\\t\\n   408\\t**The slow tier** runs each tagged namespace on its own JVM, a few at a time:\\n   409\\t\\n   410\\t```sh\\n   411\\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n   412\\t# Usage: slow-tier.sh <clone> [parallel] -- the ^:slow tests of the tagged namespaces, one JVM per namespace\\n   413\\tset -u\\n   414\\texport PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\\\"\\n   415\\tcd \\\"$1\\\" || exit 2\\n   416\\tPAR=\\\"${2:-6}\\\"\\n   417\\tmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\\n   418\\teval \\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\"\\n   419\\tOUT=\\\"$1/target-ci/slowtier\\\"; rm -rf \\\"$OUT\\\"; mkdir -p \\\"$OUT\\\"\\n   420\\trun_ns() {\\n   421\\t  n=$1; t0=$(date +%s)\\n   422\\t  clojure -M:test -i :slow -n \\\"$n\\\" > \\\"$OUT/$n.log\\\" 2>&1; rc=$?\\n   423\\t  echo \\\"$n rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-t0 )) $(grep -E \\\"^Ran \\\" \\\"$OUT/$n.log\\\" | tail -1)\\\" >> \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   424\\t}\\n   425\\texport -f run_ns; export OUT\\n   426\\techo \\\"start $(date +%H:%M:%S) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) par=$PAR\\\" > \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   427\\txargs -P \\\"$PAR\\\" -I{} bash -c \\\"run_ns {}\\\" < \\\"$HOME/ci/pertest-ns.txt\\\"\\n   428\\techo \\\"done $(date +%H:%M:%S)\\\" >> \\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\"\\n   429\\t```\\n   430\\t\\n   200\\t  the worktree). NOTE: the S1-era briefs and findings (1793294…-1793340…: the ownership map, the\\n   201\\t  inventory findings, the S1/S3 briefs, the pins/resume/expectations rounds, the S1 gate) were\\n   202\\t  absent from collab/ at archive time — likely swept by an interim bulk pass; their substance lives\\n   203\\t  in this log, the landed commits, and the gate artifacts that survived. collab/ is now empty.\\n   204\\tThe final handoff: the yang.python seat's 8.10 integration is DONE; the next seat (or this one, on\\n   205\\t  return) owns the 8.10.11 conformance evidence (bidirectional/higher-order cross-language fixtures,\\n   206\\t  bundled/linked equivalence — the entry fixture is the base), the worker-isolation debt row, and\\n   207\\t  monitoring the nightly. The standing rules: the two-tier testing policy, the dao.stream merge\\n   208\\t  precondition, the laptop-unload rule, the shared-checkout staging rule (nobody's staging area),\\n   209\\t  the slow-bodies rule for slow-guarded surfaces. Prior session log: docs/orchestrator-log.md (the\\n   210\\t  pre-handoff era) + this file. The tree: origin/master at efc99cc4.\\n   211\\t## 2026-10-31 12:5x +07 — the nightly rescheduled to 3am VIETNAM time (the owner: shiva is in Philadelphia)\\n   212\\tThe owner's correction: shiva sits in Philadelphia (EDT), so the 3am crontab fired at shiva's local\\n   213\\t  3am — the wrong window (it would also drift an hour when US DST ends). Reinstalled: the crontab\\n   214\\t  now fires HOURLY and ~/ci/nightly-full.sh carries a guard that runs the suite